WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.491 --> 00:00:16.953
walked along the main road until he spotted a footpath crossing a field.

2
00:00:16.973 --> 00:00:22.057
"Mr. Bumble brought me on that path when I came to the workhouse," he said to himself.

3
00:00:23.117 --> 00:00:26.760
To avoid being noticed, he decided to leave the main road and take the path.

4
00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:28.962
He soon reached Mrs.

5
00:00:29.002 --> 00:00:32.244
Mann's farm, where he had lived for the first ten years of his life.

6
00:00:33.424 --> 00:00:35.105
No one was stirring at this early hour.

7
00:00:36.206 --> 00:00:38.448
Oliver passed by silently and kept on walking.

8
00:00:39.509 --> 00:00:42.471
When the path ended, he found himself back on the main road.

9
00:00:43.531 --> 00:00:47.674
The sun was shining brightly now, and Oliver was still afraid someone might see him.

10
00:00:48.735 --> 00:00:50.857
So he alternately ran and hid behind bushes.

11
00:00:51.998 --> 00:00:54.940
At noon he sat down by a milestone to think about where to go.

12
00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.262
The milestone said it was seventy miles to London.

13
00:00:58.282 --> 00:01:00.724
"London!" thought Oliver.

14
00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:03.842
"Nobody could ever find me in a huge city.

15
00:01:04.862 --> 00:01:05.543
Not even Mr.

16
00:01:05.603 --> 00:01:11.547
Bumble." He had often heard the old men in the workhouse say that an enterprising boy would never

17
00:01:11.647 --> 00:01:12.427
starve in London.

18
00:01:13.408 --> 00:01:16.870
There were ways to earn a living in the city that country people couldn't even imagine.

19
00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:20.112
Oliver jumped to his feet and started walking again.

20
00:01:21.193 --> 00:01:25.016
He walked for five more miles before he realized how long it would take him to get to

21
00:01:25.076 --> 00:01:28.518
London. Sitting down to rest, he opened his bundle.

22
00:01:28.538 --> 00:01:32.368
"A clean shirt is a very comfortable thing," thought Oliver.

23
00:01:32.388 --> 00:01:35.289
"And so are two pairs of darned stockings.

24
00:01:36.369 --> 00:01:40.490
A penny and a crust of bread are good too, but they're of little help on a 65-mile

25
00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:41.591
walk in wintertime."

26
00:01:42.691 --> 00:01:44.432
Oliver walked twenty miles that day.

27
00:01:45.412 --> 00:01:49.313
He ate only the crust of dry bread and drank only a few drinks of water begged from

28
00:01:49.373 --> 00:01:50.493
cottages along the road.

29
00:01:52.154 --> 00:01:55.115
That night he went into a meadow and slept under a hay wagon.

30
00:01:56.195 --> 00:01:59.916
At first he was frightened by the wind moaning dismally over the empty fields.

31
00:02:01.056 --> 00:02:05.358
He had never felt so lonely, but exhausted from his journey, he soon fell asleep.

32
00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:09.921
The next morning he was so hungry that he had to use his penny to buy a small

33
00:02:09.961 --> 00:02:10.601
loaf of bread.

34
00:02:11.722 --> 00:02:14.663
He had walked no more than 12 miles when night closed in again.

35
00:02:15.724 --> 00:02:17.665
His feet were sore and his legs were weak.

36
00:02:18.706 --> 00:02:20.327
He spent another night outdoors.

37
00:02:21.447 --> 00:02:23.408
The days passed and Oliver kept walking.

38
00:02:24.409 --> 00:02:29.071
In some villages he saw large signs warning that beggars would be sent to jail, so he hurried

39
00:02:29.091 --> 00:02:29.932
through those villages.

40
00:02:31.048 --> 00:02:35.030
In other places he hung around the inns, hoping someone would give him something to eat.

41
00:02:36.031 --> 00:02:39.473
He begged at farmhouses, but usually the farmers threatened to set the dogs on him.

42
00:02:41.254 --> 00:02:45.216
Oliver would have starved to death without the bread and cheese given to him by a kindhearted toll

43
00:02:45.256 --> 00:02:46.537
collector and an old lady.

44
00:02:47.637 --> 00:02:51.680
On the seventh morning after he had run away, he slowly limped into a little town.

45
00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:57.523
The sun was rising as Oliver, with bleeding feet and dust-covered clothes, sat on a doorstep.

46
00:02:58.563 --> 00:02:59.424
A boy passed by.

47
00:03:00.512 --> 00:03:03.974
He returned a few minutes later and stood across the road, staring at Oliver.

48
00:03:05.055 --> 00:03:08.157
Noticing that Oliver was looking at him, the boy crossed the road.

49
00:03:09.158 --> 00:03:10.919
"Hello, my friend," said the boy.

50
00:03:10.939 --> 00:03:12.780
"What brings you here?"

51
00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:18.124
Oliver couldn't answer for a moment because he was busy staring at the boy, who was the strangest

52
00:03:18.204 --> 00:03:19.425
person he'd ever seen.

53
00:03:20.425 --> 00:03:22.847
He was definitely a boy, but he swaggered like a man.

54
00:03:24.548 --> 00:03:29.211
A hat perched precariously on top of his head, and he wore a man's coat that nearly reached

55
00:03:29.251 --> 00:03:29.652
his heels.

56
00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:33.921
The sleeves were so long that he had to roll them up to see his hands.

57
00:03:33.941 --> 00:03:39.004
"I'm hungry and tired," Oliver finally replied with tears in his eyes.

58
00:03:39.024 --> 00:03:41.625
"I've been walking for seven days."

59
00:03:41.645 --> 00:03:43.646
"Seven days!"

60
00:03:44.086 --> 00:03:44.826
exclaimed the boy.

61
00:03:44.846 --> 00:03:46.767
"That's a long time.

62
00:03:47.748 --> 00:03:49.509
If you want food, you shall have it!"

63
00:03:50.569 --> 00:03:53.790
Helping Oliver to stand up, the boy took him to a nearby shop.

64
00:03:54.751 --> 00:03:56.852
There he purchased a ham and a loaf of bread.

65
00:03:57.876 --> 00:04:01.839
Then he led Oliver to a pub, where he bought something to drink and urged Oliver to eat

66
00:04:01.879 --> 00:04:02.639
the bread and ham.

67
00:04:02.659 --> 00:04:04.380
"Going to London?"

68
00:04:04.741 --> 00:04:06.822
asked the strange boy when Oliver had finished eating.

69
00:04:06.842 --> 00:04:09.244
"Yes," answered Oliver.

70
00:04:09.264 --> 00:04:11.125
"Got any lodgings?"

71
00:04:12.906 --> 00:04:14.787
"No." "Got any money?"

72
00:04:14.807 --> 00:04:18.330
"No." The boy whistled and shook his head.

73
00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:20.251
"Do you live in London?"

74
00:04:20.611 --> 00:04:21.212
asked Oliver.

75
00:04:21.232 --> 00:04:23.013
"Yes, I do.

76
00:04:23.993 --> 00:04:26.055
I suppose you'll be wanting someplace to sleep tonight."

77
00:04:26.075 --> 00:04:28.628
"Oh, yes," replied Oliver.

78
00:04:28.648 --> 00:04:31.810
"I haven't slept under a roof since I left the country."

79
00:04:32.851 --> 00:04:34.211
"Well, don't fret about that.

80
00:04:35.152 --> 00:04:36.373
I have to be in London tonight.

81
00:04:37.393 --> 00:04:40.215
I know a respectable old gentleman who'll give you lodgings for free."

82
00:04:41.235 --> 00:04:44.377
This unexpected offer was too tempting for Oliver to pass up.

83
00:04:45.437 --> 00:04:49.380
He and the boy continued to talk, and Oliver discovered that his name was Jack Dawkins.

84
00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:53.122
"But my friends call me the Artful Dodger," said the boy.

85
00:04:54.182 --> 00:04:57.444
For some reason the Dodger didn't want to arrive in London before nightfall.

86
00:04:59.092 --> 00:05:01.855
So it was nearly eleven o'clock when they entered the great city.

87
00:05:02.876 --> 00:05:07.160
Oliver followed closely behind as his new friend led him into one of the worst parts of the

88
00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:11.404
city. Oliver had never seen a dirtier or more wretched place.

89
00:05:12.485 --> 00:05:15.368
The streets were narrow and muddy, and the air smelled of filth.

90
00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:20.312
At last the Dodger pushed open the door to an old house and whistled loudly.

91
00:05:20.332 --> 00:05:22.074
"Now then!"

92
00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:23.956
a strange voice said in reply.

93
00:05:25.036 --> 00:05:30.100
The Dodger uttered a mysterious password and then led Oliver upstairs to a dark and dirty room.

94
00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:34.983
Four boys sat at a table watching an old man cook sausages over the fire.

95
00:05:36.024 --> 00:05:38.746
The boys gathered around as the Dodger whispered to the man.

96
00:05:39.886 --> 00:05:45.350
Suddenly the Dodger said, "Fagin, this is my friend Oliver Twist," and everyone turned to look.

97
00:05:47.091 --> 00:05:51.214
Now Oliver could see that the man's matted red hair covered much of an ugly face.

98
00:05:51.234 --> 00:05:56.042
"Pleased to meet you," he said, taking Oliver's hand and bowing low.

99
00:05:57.002 --> 00:06:01.184
The boys crowded around Oliver, shaking his hands and putting their hands into his pockets.

100
00:06:02.305 --> 00:06:06.287
Fagin watched as Oliver stared at the many silk handkerchiefs hanging about the room.

101
00:06:06.307 --> 00:06:10.130
"I see you've noticed our handkerchiefs," said Fagin.

102
00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:12.891
"We're just getting them ready for the wash."

103
00:06:13.932 --> 00:06:15.653
The boys all burst into laughter.

104
00:06:16.653 --> 00:06:20.616
Oliver was puzzled, but he didn't say anything because the sausages were done and it was time to

105
00:06:20.756 --> 00:06:26.123
eat. After supper Oliver settled down on an old sack and went right to sleep on the floor.

106
00:06:27.084 --> 00:06:30.447
He could wait until tomorrow to begin his new life in this strange place.
